{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not sacrifice… that has a blemish in it.</b> And it does not say אֲשֶׁר בּוֹ מוּם, as they expounded, of blessed memory (Sifrei), that the verse comes to prohibit a transient blemish — they alluded to this in the word <b>יִהְיֶה</b>, to mean every form of existence of a blemish, whether permanent or transient. And it is further possible to say: if a limb was diagnosed in the animal as having developed a blemish, and the physicians said that it must in any case be cut out — even though they have not yet cut it, it is already disqualified. And this is what the verse says: <b>you shall not sacrifice</b>… <b>that will have a blemish in it</b> — meaning, even though at present it is not yet a blemish, since it stands to become a blemish, you shall not sacrifice it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:42.095550496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}